1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,700
(Episode 2)

2
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:06,720
It's me.

3
00:00:08,790 --> 00:00:09,990
I'll be there soon.

4
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:33,400
Three whole years.

5
00:02:35,410 --> 00:02:36,610
I'm finally back.

6
00:02:38,210 --> 00:02:39,510
Back in this living hell.

7
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:46,030
Ow! But that was so cool, Kataoka-san!

8
00:02:49,890 --> 00:02:51,090
Cut! Cut!

9
00:02:54,030 --> 00:02:55,750
Sorry, I said what I was thinking out loud.

10
00:02:58,390 --> 00:02:59,390
Hey, Eiji.

11
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:03,099
I was supposed to take down the
pursuers and say, 'Like and subscribe!'

12
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:05,760
- Wasn't that the plan?
- Please, let's do one more take!

13
00:03:05,970 --> 00:03:06,820
Forget it.

14
00:03:06,821 --> 00:03:08,220
We're done filming. That's a wrap!

15
00:03:10,990 --> 00:03:12,090
More importantly,

16
00:03:17,010 --> 00:03:18,330
since we're finally back in town,

17
00:03:19,130 --> 00:03:20,259
let's grab a drink.

18
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:21,950
Let's party hard!

19
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:31,700
"The Journey To Killing You Season 2"

20
00:04:31,790 --> 00:04:33,039
Hey, listen up.

21
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:35,590
A winning horse has an aura like no other.

22
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:39,500
The moment our eyes met in the paddock,
my gut knew that it was the one.

23
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:44,019
From the gate, the two
favorites fought for the lead.

24
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:46,570
Meanwhile, my pick was dead last.

25
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:50,700
Then, rounding the final turn, it
started surging from the outside!

26
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:53,370
Blazing down the final
stretch with incredible speed!

27
00:04:53,540 --> 00:04:55,330
Can it pull through?

28
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:56,569
Can it make it?!

29
00:04:56,570 --> 00:04:57,879
Will it pull through?

30
00:04:57,880 --> 00:04:58,880
Will it make it?!

31
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:03,520
A stunning comeback win!

32
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:08,600
Hey, you guys...

33
00:05:10,530 --> 00:05:12,020
Time for some pocket money!

34
00:05:15,850 --> 00:05:17,189
Go treat yourselves to whatever you like.

35
00:05:17,190 --> 00:05:18,540
My apologies.

36
00:05:19,230 --> 00:05:20,870
Hey, what do you feel like eating?

37
00:05:21,150 --> 00:05:23,020
- It's fine.
- Sushi! Sushi! Sushi!

38
00:05:23,030 --> 00:05:25,150
He went completely wild at the track.

39
00:05:25,730 --> 00:05:26,930
I tried to stop him.

40
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:30,280
Never mind. It's fine.

41
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:36,080
So,

42
00:05:36,790 --> 00:05:38,630
the reason you called us here...

43
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:40,810
What is this crisis facing the Kirii-gumi?

44
00:05:42,230 --> 00:05:43,230
Money.

45
00:05:45,550 --> 00:05:46,550
Six months ago,

46
00:05:48,110 --> 00:05:49,800
our parent organization, the Koutokukai,

47
00:05:50,010 --> 00:05:51,720
was taken over by the boss's son, Hanao.

48
00:05:51,930 --> 00:05:52,840
Huh?

49
00:05:52,850 --> 00:05:55,520
The head of the family isn't
old enough to retire, is he?

50
00:05:56,270 --> 00:05:57,270
Did he die?

51
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:58,800
No.

52
00:05:59,320 --> 00:06:01,590
Word is his twenty-seven-year-old
new wife begged him,

53
00:06:02,450 --> 00:06:03,950
so he relocated to Cebu Island.

54
00:06:05,570 --> 00:06:07,130
That old man sure has plenty of energy.

55
00:06:08,663 --> 00:06:11,253
When it came to his son
taking over the family,

56
00:06:12,030 --> 00:06:15,040
all the affiliates, including
us, gave our approval.

57
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:18,850
That should have been the end of it.

58
00:06:21,210 --> 00:06:22,210
Our dues...

59
00:06:23,590 --> 00:06:26,040
They raised our monthly tribute payment.

60
00:06:28,830 --> 00:06:29,830
Why the sudden hike?

61
00:06:31,970 --> 00:06:33,170
Awakuma...

62
00:06:33,550 --> 00:06:36,020
was selected for a massive
urban redevelopment project.

63
00:06:36,730 --> 00:06:37,930
Awakuma?

64
00:06:38,710 --> 00:06:39,710
That's right.

65
00:06:40,230 --> 00:06:42,300
It's your old turf, Kataoka-san.

66
00:06:44,130 --> 00:06:45,610
They're redeveloping that place, huh?

67
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:46,940
Yes.

68
00:06:47,610 --> 00:06:48,610
Because of that,

69
00:06:48,890 --> 00:06:50,840
claiming property values would surge,

70
00:06:51,470 --> 00:06:52,490
they jacked up the fee.

71
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:56,280
Even with redevelopment, it takes years.
How are you supposed to cash out right away?

72
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:57,400
Exactly.

73
00:06:57,990 --> 00:06:58,990
On top of that,

74
00:07:00,290 --> 00:07:01,490
times are tough right now.

75
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:04,690
Not only are relations with the
locals in Awakuma deteriorating,

76
00:07:05,990 --> 00:07:08,060
our business operations are struggling.

77
00:07:09,010 --> 00:07:10,830
Were those locals always that difficult?

78
00:07:15,850 --> 00:07:19,260
If business is rough,
just be straight with headquarters.

79
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:21,830
We can't go against the parent family.

80
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:24,500
- But weren't those two...
- Under the previous boss,

81
00:07:25,650 --> 00:07:28,270
the parent family and our boss

82
00:07:29,110 --> 00:07:30,590
were certainly on good terms.

83
00:07:31,990 --> 00:07:32,990
However...

84
00:07:33,970 --> 00:07:35,170
the man calling the shots now,

85
00:07:36,290 --> 00:07:37,570
the President of the Koutokukai,

86
00:07:38,070 --> 00:07:39,170
Hikari Hanao,

87
00:07:39,990 --> 00:07:42,040
and Kirii Keito, head of the Kirii-gumi...

88
00:07:43,050 --> 00:07:44,206
The two of them are like oil and water.

89
00:07:44,230 --> 00:07:45,800
Things could explode at any moment.

90
00:07:48,610 --> 00:07:49,610
If they ever cross paths,

91
00:07:49,850 --> 00:07:51,290
an all-out turf war could break out.

92
00:07:58,010 --> 00:07:59,210
And there's nothing

93
00:07:59,670 --> 00:08:01,000
we can do about it.

94
00:08:05,030 --> 00:08:06,130
Please.

95
00:08:07,550 --> 00:08:08,650
Kataoka-san.

96
00:08:10,950 --> 00:08:12,150
At this rate,

97
00:08:13,690 --> 00:08:15,640
the Koutokukai will wipe us out completely.

98
00:08:19,770 --> 00:08:20,770
We beg of you.

99
00:08:23,810 --> 00:08:25,880
Please save the Kirii-gumi.

100
00:08:37,110 --> 00:08:38,440
Good work today.

101
00:08:41,750 --> 00:08:43,050
I'm back.

102
00:08:46,110 --> 00:08:47,110
Boss.

103
00:08:47,470 --> 00:08:49,000
Thank you for working so late.

104
00:08:52,950 --> 00:08:53,950
How did it go?

105
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:05,670
I took over only to find the old
man left behind a mountain of debt.

106
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:10,920
Scraping by to pay it off
while revenues keep shrinking...

107
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,340
and now headquarters hikes our tribute.

108
00:09:16,830 --> 00:09:21,020
Even the bankers who milked us dry
turned their backs on us.

109
00:09:24,590 --> 00:09:26,520
Crooked vultures. Worse than the yakuza.

110
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:32,020
Boss, maybe we should...

111
00:09:32,670 --> 00:09:34,030
ask headquarters for an extension?

112
00:09:34,110 --> 00:09:36,900
I'd rather die than bow to them.

113
00:09:39,270 --> 00:09:40,510
Don't ever bring that up again.

114
00:09:59,530 --> 00:10:00,940
Smells awful in here.

115
00:10:04,430 --> 00:10:05,630
Did someone drop by?

116
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:07,240
No.

117
00:10:19,850 --> 00:10:21,180
A mistress's place, huh?

118
00:10:22,350 --> 00:10:24,750
She went on a trip and said we
could make ourselves at home?

119
00:10:26,090 --> 00:10:28,000
Old man Kumakura sure knows how to live.

120
00:10:30,650 --> 00:10:33,639
I get why I got called in.

121
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:35,800
Still, making a move will
have to wait until tomorrow.

122
00:10:42,650 --> 00:10:43,850
What?

123
00:10:44,570 --> 00:10:45,570
Nothing.

124
00:10:46,810 --> 00:10:49,120
You've been acting weird
ever since we arrived.

125
00:10:49,750 --> 00:10:51,840
Are you mad because I was out having fun?

126
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:52,798
I'm not mad.

127
00:10:52,822 --> 00:10:54,760
I won at the races, didn't
I? What's the problem?

128
00:10:55,590 --> 00:10:56,590
Right.

129
00:10:57,690 --> 00:11:00,730
Odajima.

130
00:11:02,700 --> 00:11:03,700
I'm not mad.

131
00:11:04,670 --> 00:11:06,880
You haven't looked me in the eye once.

132
00:11:11,070 --> 00:11:12,070
Please take that off.

133
00:11:13,450 --> 00:11:15,340
You'll wrinkle the suit.

134
00:11:16,270 --> 00:11:17,400
Oh.

135
00:11:19,110 --> 00:11:21,070
We wore nothing but
Hawaiian shirts on the island.

136
00:11:21,353 --> 00:11:23,713
Putting on a suit after so long
makes me look pretty sharp.

137
00:11:28,710 --> 00:11:29,710
Hm?

138
00:11:31,190 --> 00:11:32,190
Ah...

139
00:11:33,030 --> 00:11:34,230
So that's what it is.

140
00:11:36,190 --> 00:11:37,390
Could it be...

141
00:11:38,950 --> 00:11:40,980
seeing me in a suit got you flustered?

142
00:11:45,780 --> 00:11:46,980
I am not flustered.

143
00:11:48,130 --> 00:11:49,500
- I'll run the bath.
- Okay.

144
00:11:50,230 --> 00:11:51,420
Make it piping hot.

145
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:53,270
My grandfather was old-school Edo.

146
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:55,300
If the bath isn't
scalding, it doesn't count.

147
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:56,550
That's a family rule.

148
00:11:56,590 --> 00:11:57,600
A family rule.

149
00:11:57,670 --> 00:11:58,670
I know.

150
00:12:13,710 --> 00:12:14,710
Odajima.

151
00:12:15,730 --> 00:12:17,030
It's Kataoka-san.

152
00:12:17,590 --> 00:12:18,980
So handsome.

153
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:31,710
The water temperature is
set to forty-two degrees.

154
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:37,390
Good.

155
00:12:38,210 --> 00:12:39,210
Let's head out.

156
00:12:50,290 --> 00:12:51,840
Just as I thought.

157
00:13:09,810 --> 00:13:10,810
Kataoka...

158
00:13:16,550 --> 00:13:18,380
That look on your face...

159
00:13:20,510 --> 00:13:21,510
It's magnificent.

160
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:19,760
Excuse me.

161
00:14:23,530 --> 00:14:25,420
Word is Kataoka's back.

162
00:14:26,730 --> 00:14:27,730
Kataoka?

163
00:14:28,650 --> 00:14:29,850
Didn't he leave the syndicate

164
00:14:30,190 --> 00:14:31,680
to play house with his little hubby?

165
00:14:50,170 --> 00:14:51,720
Good for him.

166
00:14:53,370 --> 00:14:54,670
He went legit,

167
00:14:55,130 --> 00:14:57,920
and now he's meddling
in yakuza affairs again?

168
00:15:00,030 --> 00:15:02,060
I love that shameless audacity.

169
00:15:13,090 --> 00:15:14,090
Good morning!

170
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:17,820
- Huh?
- Boss Kumakura sent me to drive for you!

171
00:15:17,990 --> 00:15:19,330
I'm Kazuki!

172
00:15:20,490 --> 00:15:21,690
- Please, get in!
- All right.

173
00:15:22,330 --> 00:15:24,210
- You're full of energy, aren't you?
- Yes, sir!

174
00:15:26,910 --> 00:15:27,910
Right this way!

175
00:15:33,117 --> 00:15:33,918
(Odajima and the boss are back.
Pick them up here tomorrow at 10:00.

176
00:15:33,942 --> 00:15:34,786
Don't ask questions. Just
follow Kataoka's orders.)

177
00:15:34,810 --> 00:15:36,746
(Understood! I've already met up
with Kataoka-san and Odajima-san!)

178
00:15:36,770 --> 00:15:40,020
Four generations of pride,
and look what we've become.

179
00:15:43,710 --> 00:15:44,710
Boss...

180
00:15:45,170 --> 00:15:47,130
Maybe we should talk
to headquarters after all...

181
00:15:48,910 --> 00:15:50,240
Don't make me repeat myself.

182
00:15:51,010 --> 00:15:52,730
How many years have you been in the yakuza?

183
00:15:54,010 --> 00:15:55,620
Our pride is our life.

184
00:15:56,970 --> 00:15:59,770
Even for a boss, show a hint of
weakness and they'll devour you alive.

185
00:16:09,570 --> 00:16:10,980
Especially that bastard.

186
00:16:14,470 --> 00:16:15,470
Kid.

187
00:16:15,910 --> 00:16:17,880
- Take us here.
- Yes, sir!

188
00:16:22,170 --> 00:16:23,170
Hm?

189
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:25,250
Thank you very much!

190
00:16:28,330 --> 00:16:31,060
Is the AC too cold or too warm?

191
00:16:31,070 --> 00:16:32,950
It's fine. Just right.

192
00:16:40,350 --> 00:16:43,050
- Something on your mind, kid?
- N-No, nothing!

193
00:16:44,290 --> 00:16:45,730
Speak up if you need to take a dump.

194
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,290
N-No, it's not that...

195
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:54,510
Better spit it out before
he loses his temper.

196
00:16:54,760 --> 00:16:58,610
Boss Kumakura told me to keep
my mouth shut and just drive, but...

197
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:04,729
Ah, I can't hold it in anymore!

198
00:17:04,730 --> 00:17:06,100
I just have to say it!

199
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:09,370
I'm Kataoka-san's biggest fan!

200
00:17:12,230 --> 00:17:13,760
Hey, did you hear that, Odajima?

201
00:17:14,490 --> 00:17:15,490
I've still got it.

202
00:17:16,630 --> 00:17:17,630
Sure.

203
00:17:18,670 --> 00:17:19,670
And also...

204
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:21,750
Odajima-san, I'm
a huge fan of yours too!

205
00:17:21,860 --> 00:17:22,860
Huh?

206
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:25,000
Of course I follow...

207
00:17:26,350 --> 00:17:27,860
'KinRen'!

208
00:17:29,490 --> 00:17:31,419
KinRen?

209
00:17:31,536 --> 00:17:33,005
Two hundred thousand followers!

210
00:17:33,030 --> 00:17:34,920
This is insane!

211
00:17:35,116 --> 00:17:38,086
I can't believe I'm driving for KinRen!

212
00:17:38,730 --> 00:17:39,730
Keep it down, will you?

213
00:17:40,370 --> 00:17:41,390
Is this...

214
00:17:41,850 --> 00:17:43,360
Looking good! Very nice.

215
00:17:48,590 --> 00:17:50,060
Hey, Odajima, dance a little more.

216
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:51,400
Okay.

217
00:17:54,370 --> 00:17:56,599
Yes, yes, yes!

218
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:57,600
Awesome.

219
00:17:58,690 --> 00:17:59,840
Looking good.

220
00:18:01,660 --> 00:18:03,059
Did you publish that video?

221
00:18:03,060 --> 00:18:04,096
The whole world can see it.

222
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:05,500
I even monetized it.

223
00:18:06,810 --> 00:18:07,979
By the way,

224
00:18:07,980 --> 00:18:09,730
why is it called 'KinRen'?

225
00:18:10,290 --> 00:18:12,400
Because I'm Kinji, and he's Ren.

226
00:18:13,570 --> 00:18:14,970
Ah, makes sense.

227
00:18:17,530 --> 00:18:19,260
- Time to roll.
- Yeah.

228
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:57,120
There's two hundred million here.

229
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:58,500
I'm leaving the syndicate.

230
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,460
It's all yours.

231
00:19:25,220 --> 00:19:26,690
- Thanks.
- Yes, sir!

232
00:19:27,860 --> 00:19:29,270
What kind of place is this?

233
00:19:30,040 --> 00:19:31,040
A diner.

234
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:32,580
It's ridiculously run-down.

235
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:34,460
You sure don't hold back, do you?

236
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:35,840
I'm Kazuki!

237
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:40,510
Go grab a coffee somewhere nearby.

238
00:19:40,740 --> 00:19:41,740
Whoa!

239
00:19:42,300 --> 00:19:43,300
Thank you so much!

240
00:19:43,930 --> 00:19:45,230
- Let's go.
- Right.

241
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:52,680
Yo.

242
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:56,540
Haven't seen you around.

243
00:19:57,620 --> 00:19:59,410
I don't waste my breath on punks.

244
00:19:59,820 --> 00:20:00,820
Get lost.

245
00:20:15,060 --> 00:20:16,800
Don't be an idiot.

246
00:20:17,090 --> 00:20:19,770
Forget breasts, it's all about the ass!

247
00:20:19,840 --> 00:20:22,380
Right? A tight one, especially.

248
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:26,010
See, you get it! Ass reigns supreme.

249
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:29,680
My wife might be flat-chested,
but that ass is out of this world.

250
00:20:30,390 --> 00:20:31,786
And this right here is my lovely wife.

251
00:20:31,810 --> 00:20:33,010
Kataoka-san...

252
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:43,120
I see.

253
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:46,090
So you're Kataoka.

254
00:20:49,660 --> 00:20:51,580
You're looking more like
your old man every day.

255
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:56,200
Yeah?

256
00:20:56,660 --> 00:20:58,100
Do I really look that much like him?

257
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:05,520
What you came here to dig up

258
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:07,500
is intel on the Koutokukai, right?

259
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:16,010
They're dangerous.

260
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:19,630
Hanao took over as boss six months ago,

261
00:21:21,020 --> 00:21:22,870
and he completely ditched the old ways.

262
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:24,960
He overhauled how they make their money.

263
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:29,650
To get what he wants,

264
00:21:30,860 --> 00:21:32,060
he stops at nothing.

265
00:21:34,740 --> 00:21:38,050
He poached an executive
named Ihashi from another crew

266
00:21:39,320 --> 00:21:41,030
to be his right-hand man,

267
00:21:41,280 --> 00:21:42,690
running the syndicate's finances.

268
00:21:45,880 --> 00:21:47,730
Now the cash is multiplying,

269
00:21:48,780 --> 00:21:50,390
and their power is skyrocketing.

270
00:21:51,740 --> 00:21:53,430
Like a monstrous beast.

271
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:56,180
A beast, huh?

272
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:12,170
Word is the Koutokukai's next prey

273
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,510
is Awakuma, right before
redevelopment begins.

274
00:22:17,780 --> 00:22:19,080
Awakuma...

275
00:22:20,260 --> 00:22:24,549
A billion brought in from illegal casinos. Seven
hundred million from the waste management bid.

276
00:22:24,550 --> 00:22:26,510
Eighty million in tribute
from branch families...

277
00:22:28,580 --> 00:22:30,890
No matter how many designer bags I send,

278
00:22:31,200 --> 00:22:33,810
those women in Ginza
keep sending them back.

279
00:22:34,540 --> 00:22:36,250
Why aren't I popular?

280
00:22:40,086 --> 00:22:42,216
I'm such a high-quality man.

281
00:22:44,690 --> 00:22:46,500
What do you think, Ihashi?

282
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:49,569
My looks and personality are top-tier.

283
00:22:49,570 --> 00:22:50,720
Not to mention,

284
00:22:50,940 --> 00:22:52,040
I'm loaded.

285
00:22:53,780 --> 00:22:55,569
That lies outside my area of expertise.

286
00:22:55,570 --> 00:22:56,780
I wouldn't know.

287
00:23:02,300 --> 00:23:04,020
Speaking of which, that underling of yours.

288
00:23:04,860 --> 00:23:06,250
How dare he cook the books?

289
00:23:10,100 --> 00:23:12,750
After I sliced off four of his fingers,

290
00:23:13,740 --> 00:23:14,820
he confessed to everything.

291
00:23:17,380 --> 00:23:19,490
Claimed he acted entirely alone.

292
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:25,030
He still had six left. Spineless coward.

293
00:23:29,360 --> 00:23:31,350
I take full responsibility. My apologies.

294
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:33,400
Hey.

295
00:23:33,920 --> 00:23:36,390
Modern incinerators are truly impressive.

296
00:23:37,740 --> 00:23:40,130
They dispose of a corpse
without leaving a trace of bone.

297
00:23:41,380 --> 00:23:43,910
The remaining ash gets mixed into concrete

298
00:23:44,760 --> 00:23:46,390
to form the foundations of skyscrapers.

299
00:23:51,300 --> 00:23:52,870
Regarding your earlier question...

300
00:23:53,420 --> 00:23:56,500
I believe no woman would fall for a man
whose heart already belongs elsewhere.

301
00:23:56,970 --> 00:23:57,970
Belongs elsewhere?

302
00:24:01,350 --> 00:24:02,350
Ah.

303
00:24:03,620 --> 00:24:04,920
You're right.

304
00:24:14,680 --> 00:24:16,570
My one true love is this city.

305
00:24:18,700 --> 00:24:20,570
I will possess it all.

306
00:24:22,240 --> 00:24:23,790
And anyone who stands in my way...

307
00:24:25,540 --> 00:24:26,810
I'll slaughter them.

308
00:24:28,420 --> 00:24:29,420
Mister.

309
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:31,200
Hey, mister...

310
00:24:33,250 --> 00:24:34,250
He's fast asleep.

311
00:24:35,760 --> 00:24:37,800
Hey, you'll catch a cold
sleeping there, old-timer.

312
00:24:45,640 --> 00:24:47,370
He said I look more like my old man.

313
00:24:48,400 --> 00:24:49,880
Not that I have many memories of him.

314
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:53,070
I think it was during a turf war...

315
00:24:54,760 --> 00:24:55,960
Killed in action.

316
00:25:08,320 --> 00:25:09,320
All right.

317
00:25:09,940 --> 00:25:10,940
Let's head out.

318
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:13,440
Where are we going?

319
00:25:13,900 --> 00:25:15,370
Where else? Obviously...

320
00:25:16,560 --> 00:25:18,050
The Koutokukai headquarters.

321
00:25:18,900 --> 00:25:20,140
To pay their president a visit.

322
00:25:23,540 --> 00:25:24,690
Thanks for the meal.

323
00:25:24,730 --> 00:25:25,730
Please get in!

324
00:25:25,980 --> 00:25:27,020
No need for the car.

325
00:25:27,110 --> 00:25:28,490
- Huh?
- We'll walk.

326
00:25:29,840 --> 00:25:31,280
It's right around the corner anyway.

327
00:25:31,820 --> 00:25:33,870
Then I'll park and catch up right away!

328
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:36,310
- Kataoka-san.
- Yeah?

329
00:25:37,110 --> 00:25:38,110
Kataoka-san!

330
00:25:38,140 --> 00:25:39,556
Storming headquarters
like this is reckless!

331
00:25:39,580 --> 00:25:42,160
Storming? Don't make it sound so violent.

332
00:25:42,760 --> 00:25:44,436
We're just dropping by
to talk. A friendly chat.

333
00:25:44,460 --> 00:25:45,000
Still...

334
00:25:45,040 --> 00:25:47,500
We left the syndicate. We're civilians now.

335
00:25:47,540 --> 00:25:48,990
That excuse won't protect us.

336
00:25:49,740 --> 00:25:51,070
You worry too much.

337
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:58,800
What will you do if they take me hostage?

338
00:26:09,190 --> 00:26:10,750
Kataoka-san!

339
00:26:13,860 --> 00:26:14,910
I won't let that happen.

340
00:26:16,320 --> 00:26:18,120
This time, I will protect
you no matter what.

341
00:26:19,620 --> 00:26:21,130
In life and death, we stick together.

342
00:26:26,160 --> 00:26:28,160
Come to think of it, I
don't think I ever told you

343
00:26:28,820 --> 00:26:30,750
the reason I married
you in the first place.

344
00:26:35,060 --> 00:26:36,590
I'll tell you when we get back.

345
00:26:38,380 --> 00:26:39,380
Ren.

346
00:26:54,230 --> 00:26:55,740
Odajima!

347
00:27:03,990 --> 00:27:05,869
Renren... I mean,

348
00:27:05,870 --> 00:27:08,280
Odajima-san, are you all right?!

349
00:27:08,670 --> 00:27:09,710
- After them!
- But...

350
00:27:09,790 --> 00:27:11,410
- Go, now!
- Yes, sir!

351
00:27:26,680 --> 00:27:27,900
(Next Episode Preview)

352
00:27:27,940 --> 00:27:28,940
You guys...

353
00:27:29,380 --> 00:27:30,980
Were you being targeted from the start?!

354
00:27:31,560 --> 00:27:33,626
Around here, the only crew reckless
enough to pull off a kidnapping

355
00:27:33,650 --> 00:27:35,110
is VOID.

356
00:27:35,400 --> 00:27:36,820
If we make one wrong move,

357
00:27:36,990 --> 00:27:39,600
Kataoka-san might never come back.

358
00:27:40,440 --> 00:27:41,280
What do you want from me?

359
00:27:41,370 --> 00:27:43,130
Are you telling me to
beg that guy for help?

360
00:27:43,160 --> 00:27:44,410
That guy...

361
00:27:44,790 --> 00:27:47,230
- He's out of control again, isn't he?
- Where is Kataoka-san?

362
00:27:47,910 --> 00:27:49,050
Don't push your luck.

363
00:27:49,160 --> 00:27:50,240
Odajima.

364
00:27:51,040 --> 00:27:52,040
This is bad.

365
00:27:52,860 --> 00:27:54,360
It's all

366
00:27:54,720 --> 00:27:56,270
under my control.
